{"raw": {"https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204689": {"title": "Assistant Director of Residence Life", "description": "Immaculata University\nJob Posting: Assistant Director of Residence Life Immaculata University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Director of Residence Life Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Director of Residence Life Category: Administrative Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: VP of Student Development and Engagement Locations: Malvern, PA Posted: Sep 10, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full Time Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 204689 Share About Immaculata University: Immaculata University seeks candidates who are passionate about upholding the value of higher education while fostering institutional excellence. Immaculata University is a comprehensive, co-ed institution of higher learning that has emphasized academic success, student outcomes and faith-based values for more than 100 years. Offering more than 75 in-demand undergraduate, graduate and certificate programs, Immaculata University provides attainable education, personal support and meaningful career pathways to tomorrow's leaders who are focused on intellectual, personal, professional and spiritual growth. Immaculata's expansive suburban campus is located in renowned Chester County, Pennsylvania, 30 miles west of Philadelphia. Why Immaculata University is the Perfect Workplace for you: Collegial Atmosphere, caring leadership, work/life balance. Mission-driven values supported by five core values: faith, community, knowledge, virtue and service. Generous paid time off benefits. Tuition Assistance: You, your spouse, and your eligible dependent children can receive tuition assistance at IU.\u00a0 Your dependent children are also eligible for tuition assistance at other institutions via the Tuition Exchange program. Health. Life, and Disability Insurance: Prescription, Dental, Vision, and Life Insurance; Disability benefits, Flexible Spending Account and Health Savings Account. Retirement Plan: Generous retirement plan to help you save for your future. Job Description: The Assistant Director of Residence Life positions are responsible for shared management of all functions of residence hall(s) of approximately 500 students and supervising a staff of approximately 15-17 resident assistants. This position coordinates complex housing programs, hears students conduct cases, conducts regular staff and supervisory meetings, responds to emergency situations, and determines course of action. This position serves as a liaison between Residence Life, Student Life, Student Affairs and Safety departments. The Assistant Director is also responsible for shared on-call responsibilities.\u00a0 This position reports to the Associate Dean of Students, Residence Life and Housing. Responsibilities: Supervise staff of resident assistants including recruitment, selection, training, ongoing supervision and evaluation, of Student Leaders (with emphasis on Resident Assistant Staff) and their retention. Conduct weekly supervisory meetings with student staff, responsible for the planning, implementation, and assessment of training and on-going development for the Resident Assistant staff. Respond to students issue calls, emergencies, crises within residential facilities and determine appropriate courses of action / resolution. Responsible for housing assignment process, openings, closings, vacation breaks manage move in / out / and associated housing changes. Designated to act and make determinations of appropriate actions relative to Student Code of Conduct violations, serves as disciplinary hearing officer. Responsible for use and monitoring of budgeting of residence hall funds, oversees and assumes responsibility for programming budget and funds for assigned residence halls. Serve as primary residential student resource and provides personal counseling / advisement for residents and refers sensitive matters as appropriate. Monitor the physical condition of building on a regular basis and works with appropriate departments on problem resolution to ensure a safe, clean and welcoming environment for student residents. Coordinate summer housing operations and supervises summer student staff. Assist the Director with long range planning including housing occupancy predictions and strategies. Serve as advisor to Residence Council. Participate in the planning and implementation of New Student Orientation as it pertains to Residence Life and Housing responsibilities, and other duties as assigned. Develop and provide ongoing education and awareness to student population of University resources for helping students with academic, career, and personal concerns and to make referrals when appropriate. Participate in IU wide events in support of residence housing such as open houses, parents' weekend, new student orientation (NSO), etc. Serve on University committees, task forces, and projects as designated. Participate in the on-call duty rotation for crisis response. There are two positions for Assistant Director with cross over duties, but each has specific focus areas. This position will have specific focus on Resident Education which includes: Oversee the development and implementation of the residence education model for Residence Life and Housing. Communicate with appropriate campus constituents to create awareness, collaboration, and strategies for implementation. Coordinate the planning, implementation, and assessment of community building through hall programs and initiatives. Assist in the maintenance of the Residence Life and Housing digital resources, social media networks, bulletin boards and postings for areas of primary responsibility as applicable. Immaculata University is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. Requirements: Minimum Requirements: Master's degree in Higher Education, Student Personnel Administration or related field preferred, Bachelors degree required. At least 1 - 3 years of experience in residential programming, preferably in a college/university setting, with supervisory experience strongly preferred. Possess excellent oral and written communication skills, the ability to work with time sensitive projects in a fast-paced environment, and the ability to multi-task while remaining pleasant and professional. Computer skills including all Microsoft office, housing management systems, previous experience with Banner preferred. Must possess a valid driver's license and maintain a clean driving record. Demonstrated commitment to inclusiveness and ability to interact positively with a diverse student population. Ability to organize and coordinate work effectively and handle administrative details independently. Ability to manage staff including hiring, evaluating, supervising and providing ongoing feedback. Ability to plan, execute, evaluate and revise activities to reach the long- and short-term goals of the Residence Life department and the University. Understanding of and commitment to student development theory and approaches to learning. Ability to effectively manage crisis response, interpret and use University policy and manage budgeted resources. Evening, on call and weekend work required. A meal plan is not included in this position. Additional Information: Special Requirements Background check required after a conditional job offer is made. Consideration of the background check will be tailored to the requirements of the job. Application Instructions: Required Documents: Resume Cover Letter Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Immaculata University 1145 KING ROAD IMMACULATA, PA. 19345"}, "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204115": {"title": "Assistant to the Director of Clinical Training", "description": "Immaculata University\nJob Posting: Assistant to the Director of Clinical Training Immaculata University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant to the Director of Clinical Training Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant to the Director of Clinical Training Category: Administrative Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Graduate Department of Psychology and Counseling Locations: Malvern, PA Posted: Aug 25, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part Time Non Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 204115 Share About Immaculata University: Immaculata University seeks candidates who are passionate about upholding the value of higher education while fostering institutional excellence. Immaculata University is a comprehensive, co-ed institution of higher learning that has emphasized academic success, student outcomes and faith-based values for more than 100 years. Offering more than 75 in-demand undergraduate, graduate and certificate programs, Immaculata University provides attainable education, personal support and meaningful career pathways to tomorrow's leaders who are focused on intellectual, personal, professional and spiritual growth. Immaculata's expansive suburban campus is located in renowned Chester County, Pennsylvania, 30 miles west of Philadelphia. Why Immaculata University is the Perfect Workplace for you: Collegial Atmosphere, caring leadership, work/life balance. Mission-driven values supported by five core values: faith, community, knowledge, virtue and service. Generous paid time off benefits. Tuition Assistance: You, your spouse, and your eligible dependent children can receive tuition assistance at IU.\u00a0 Your dependent children are also eligible for tuition assistance at other institutions via the Tuition Exchange program. Retirement Plan: Generous retirement plan to help you save for your future. Job Description: We are seeking a detail oriented and professional Assistant to the Director of Clinical Training (DCT) within a doctoral psychology training program. This position involves assisting with the internship application process for doctoral students pursuing APA accredited internships and supporting various administrative and educational initiatives related to clinical training. The position is 20 hours per week, from September 1 to June 1, with flexible hours\u00a0except during scheduled in person fall workshops. Responsibilities: Reviewing and proofreading internship application materials, including CVs, cover letters, essays, and supplemental documents for clarity, formatting, grammar, and professionalism. Assists with organizing and coordinating internship preparation activities, such as interview workshops, mock interviews, informational meetings, and application timelines. Tracking student application progress, maintaining organizational systems and spreadsheets, communicating with students regarding deadlines and materials, and assisting with scheduling related activities and events. The individual in this role will develop familiarity with APPIC, APA internship standards, and the doctoral internship application process. Ideal candidates are organized, dependable, proactive, and interested in graduate training, psychology, higher education, or academic administration. Immaculata University is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. Requirements: Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree required; background in psychology, education, counseling, English, communications, or a related field preferred Strong written communication, proofreading, and editing skills Excellent attention to detail and organizational abilities Ability to manage multiple deadlines and tasks simultaneously in a fast paced environment Professional interpersonal and communication skills, particularly when working with doctoral level students, faculty, and training sites Ability to provide constructive feedback in a supportive and professional manner Strong proficiency with Microsoft Office, Google Workspace, and general administrative technology platforms Ability to maintain strict confidentiality and appropriately handle sensitive student, academic, and training related information Understanding of professional boundaries, discretion, and ethical conduct within an academic and clinical training environment Preferred Requirements: Prior administrative or academic support experience Experience reviewing professional or academic writing materials Familiarity with graduate education, psychology training, or internship application processes Experience coordinating workshops, events, or student programming Strong formatting skills for professional documents and application materials Previous experience with editing, administrative support, student support services, or psychology related settings is preferred Additional Information: Special Requirements Background check required after a conditional job offer is made. Consideration of the background check will be tailored to the requirements of the job. Application Instructions: Required Documents: Resume Cover Letter Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Immaculata University 1145 KING ROAD IMMACULATA, PA. 19345"}, "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205901": {"title": "Network Administrator", "description": "Immaculata University\nJob Posting: Network Administrator Immaculata University \n\tJob Posting: Network Administrator Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Network Administrator Category: Administrative Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Off of Technology Service Locations: Malvern, PA Posted: Oct 19, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full Time Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 205901 Share About Immaculata University: Immaculata University seeks candidates who are passionate about upholding the value of higher education while fostering institutional excellence. Immaculata University is a comprehensive, co-ed institution of higher learning that has emphasized academic success, student outcomes and faith-based values for more than 100 years. Offering more than 75 in-demand undergraduate, graduate and certificate programs, Immaculata University provides attainable education, personal support and meaningful career pathways to tomorrow's leaders who are focused on intellectual, personal, professional and spiritual growth. Immaculata's expansive suburban campus is located in renowned Chester County, Pennsylvania, 30 miles west of Philadelphia. Why Immaculata University is the Perfect Workplace for you: Collegial Atmosphere, caring leadership, work/life balance. Mission-driven values supported by five core values: faith, community, knowledge, virtue and service. Generous paid time off benefits. Tuition Assistance: You, your spouse, and your eligible dependent children can receive tuition assistance at IU.\u00a0 Your dependent children are also eligible for tuition assistance at other institutions via the Tuition Exchange program. Health. Life, and Disability Insurance: Prescription, Dental, Vision, and Life Insurance; Disability benefits, Flexible Spending Account and Health Savings Account. Retirement Plan: Generous retirement plan to help you save for your future. Job Description: The network administrator, reporting directly to the director of technology services, is responsible for the day-to-day operation, maintenance and security of the University's campus network, which includes Cisco switching and routing infrastructure, Fortinet FortiGate firewalls, VLAN design that segments campus traffic and the wireless network and access points that serve students, faculty, staff and guests. The network administrator applies an understanding of network environments to keep the network reliable, secure and well documented and supports related server, telecom and data center operations. Responsibilities: Cisco Switching and Routing Configure, maintain and troubleshoot Cisco switches and routers, including access-layer, distribution and core devices. Perform scheduled Cisco IOS / NX-OS / IOS-XE software upgrades following vendor guidance and approved change windows. Maintain Spanning Tree Protocol (STP) settings, port security, link aggregation (EtherChannel) and Power over Ethernet (PoE) budgets. Replace failed hardware, manage spares and coordinate vendor support (Cisco TAC) and warranty/maintenance contracts. FortiGate Firewalls and Network Security Administer FortiGate firewalls: firewall policies, NAT, address and service objects, and security profiles (IPS, web filtering, antivirus, application control). Configure and support site-to-site and remote-access VPNs. Maintain firewall high availability (HA) and confirm failover operates as designed. Plan and perform FortiOS firmware upgrades following Fortinet's documented upgrade path, with configuration backups taken before every change. Review firewall logs and alerts (e.g., FortiAnalyzer or syslog) and respond to suspicious activity. Monitor Cisco and Fortinet security advisories (PSIRT) and apply critical patches promptly. Design, create, and maintain effective Access Control Lists (ACL) to ensure appropriate network security VLANs and Network Segmentation Design, create and maintain VLANs to separate traffic types (e.g., administrative, academic, student/residential, guest, voice, security cameras, building systems and network management). Configure 802.1Q trunk and access ports, native VLANs and allowed-VLAN lists on switches, firewalls and wireless infrastructure. Maintain inter-VLAN routing and the firewall policies that control traffic between VLANs. Coordinate DHCP scopes, DHCP relay (IP helper) and IP addressing for each VLAN. Keep an up-to-date VLAN and IP address register (VLAN ID, name, subnet, gateway, purpose and location). Wireless Network and Access Points Install, configure and maintain wireless access points and wireless controllers or cloud management platforms. Map each SSID to its correct VLAN and security settings, including WPA2/WPA3-Enterprise with 802.1X/RADIUS authentication and a segmented guest network. Plan AP placement, channels, and transmit power; perform wireless site surveys and resolve coverage, interference and capacity issues. Verify switch-port configuration, PoE availability and cabling for every access point. Update AP and controller firmware and track AP inventory, locations and status. Systems, Support, and Operations Support server and network services, including DNS, DHCP, LDAP and Active Directory integration. Ensure network device configurations and critical files are backed up routinely and stored securely. Monitor network health, performance and availability and respond to outages to maintain continuity of University operations. Provide Tier 2/3 technical support to users and the IT help desk for network and connectivity issues. Deliver responsive, courteous service to students, faculty and staff across campus. Documentation and Projects Create and maintain network documentation: topology diagrams, VLAN/IP records, firewall rule rationale, wireless coverage maps and standard operating procedures. Follow change-management procedures for configuration changes and maintenance. Serve as project lead for network, wireless and security infrastructure projects. Perform other related duties as assigned. Requirements: Minimum Requirements: Degree in information technology, networking or a related field and at least 2 years of related experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Working knowledge of Cisco switching and routing, including VLANs, 802.1Q trunking, inter-VLAN routing and STP. Experience administering enterprise firewalls; FortiGate / FortiOS experience strongly preferred. Experience with enterprise wireless controllers and access points, including SSID-to-VLAN mapping and 802.1X authentication. Knowledge of TCP/IP, subnetting, DNS, DHCP, LDAP and Active Directory. Cisco CCNA certification, or the ability to obtain it within 12 months of hire. Working knowledge of current Microsoft Windows operating systems. Understanding of network security practices, including access control, password and credential management, and file protection. Ability to troubleshoot end-user connectivity issues at the desktop and device level. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to listen carefully and explain technical information clearly and concisely. Demonstrated ability to defuse and resolve customer complaints professionally. Preferred Requirements: Experience in technology services within higher education. Fortinet certification (e.g., Fortinet Certified Professional ? Network Security, formerly NSE 4). Experience with VMware or other virtualization platforms. Experience with network monitoring tools and centralized logging. Hands-on experience with a variety of computer hardware, software, and peripherals, including Microsoft 365. ITIL Foundation certification. Additional Information: Special Requirements Background check required after a conditional job offer is made. Consideration of the background check will be tailored to the requirements of the job. Application Instructions: Required Documents: Resume Cover Letter Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Immaculata University 1145 KING ROAD IMMACULATA, PA. 19345"}, "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204724": {"title": "Part Time Head Coach Men's and Women's Tennis", "description": "Immaculata University\nJob Posting: Part Time Head Coach Men's and Women's Tennis Immaculata University \n\tJob Posting: Part Time Head Coach Men's and Women's Tennis Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Part Time Head Coach Men's and Women's Tennis Category: Administrative Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Athletics Locations: Malvern, PA Posted: Sep 11, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Contract Position\u00a0ID: 204724 Share About Immaculata University: Immaculata University seeks candidates who are passionate about upholding the value of higher education while fostering institutional excellence. Immaculata University is a comprehensive, co-ed institution of higher learning that has emphasized academic success, student outcomes and faith-based values for more than 100 years. Offering more than 75 in-demand undergraduate, graduate and certificate programs, Immaculata University provides attainable education, personal support and meaningful career pathways to tomorrow's leaders who are focused on intellectual, personal, professional and spiritual growth. Immaculata's expansive suburban campus is located in renowned Chester County, Pennsylvania, 30 miles west of Philadelphia. Why Immaculata University is the Perfect Workplace for you: Collegial Atmosphere, caring leadership, work/life balance. Mission-driven values supported by five core values: faith, community, knowledge, virtue and service. Job Description: The Head Coach leads and maintains an effective Division III sports program through recruiting, on-court/field teaching techniques, scheduling and maintaining a competitive conference season, maintain NCAA standards, budget management, fundraising, as well as promoting the sport throughout the University and local community. The Head Coach is responsible for all aspect that relate to the sports program including the ongoing development of the student athlete, promoting their physical, academic, and social growth in line with the mission and values of the University.\u00a0 The Head Coach is expected to serve as the public face of the program, creating and maintaining a positive public image while recruiting and training student-athletes to compete at the highest level possible. This position reports to the Athletics Director. Responsibilities: Develop and implement a comprehensive training program to enhance players' skills, knowledge, and performance in tennis. Plan and conduct regular practices, focusing on individual and team development, strategy implementation, and game preparation. Provide instruction and guidance to players on proper techniques, rules, and strategies specific to collegiate tennis. Teach and set expectations of appropriate team conduct during competition, travel, practice and at all University events, and at any other times when the team is representing the University. Evaluate players' abilities and provide constructive feedback to help them improve their skills and performance. Develop game plans and strategies to maximize the team's chances of success during competitions. Ensure compliance with Atlantic East Conference and university policies and procedures. Meet student athlete recruiting goals as established by the Director of Athletics and Recreation. Achieve and maintain certification for CPR/AED and First Aid. Monitor team fundraising account and ensure accurate. coordination and reporting of funds usage and maintenance in accordance with university guidelines. Develop and maintain alumni relations for the promotion of the program. Represent the University and its athletics program, with honesty, integrity, and sportsmanship at all times, to various institutional programs and students, parents and families, the general public, alumni and external agencies. Work with various departments and personnel at the university to aid in the development of a positive student-athlete experience. Other duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics and Recreation. Immaculata University is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. Requirements: Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree with successful collegiate or high school tennis coaching experience. Additional Information: Special Requirements Background check required after a conditional job offer is made. Consideration of the background check will be tailored to the requirements of the job. Application Instructions: Required Documents: Resume Cover Letter Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Immaculata University 1145 KING ROAD IMMACULATA, PA. 19345"}, "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204726": {"title": "Part-Time Head Coach - Women's Lacrosse", "description": "Immaculata University\nJob Posting: Part-Time Head Coach - Women's Lacrosse Immaculata University \n\tJob Posting: Part-Time Head Coach - Women's Lacrosse Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Part-Time Head Coach - Women's Lacrosse Category: Administrative Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Athletics Locations: Malvern, PA Posted: Sep 11, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Contract Position\u00a0ID: 204726 Share About Immaculata University: Immaculata University seeks candidates who are passionate about upholding the value of higher education while fostering institutional excellence. Immaculata University is a comprehensive, co-ed institution of higher learning that has emphasized academic success, student outcomes and faith-based values for more than 100 years. Offering more than 75 in-demand undergraduate, graduate and certificate programs, Immaculata University provides attainable education, personal support and meaningful career pathways to tomorrow's leaders who are focused on intellectual, personal, professional and spiritual growth. Immaculata's expansive suburban campus is located in renowned Chester County, Pennsylvania, 30 miles west of Philadelphia. Why Immaculata University is the Perfect Workplace for you: Collegial Atmosphere, caring leadership, work/life balance. Mission-driven values supported by five core values: faith, community, knowledge, virtue and service. Job Description: The Head Coach leads and maintains an effective Division III athletics program through recruiting, on- field teaching techniques, scheduling and maintaining a competitive conference and non-conference schedule, maintain NCAA standards, budget management, fundraising, as well as promoting the sport throughout the University and local community. The Head Coach is responsible for all aspects that relate to the women's lacrosse program including the ongoing development of the student athlete, promoting their physical, academic, and social growth in line with the mission and values of the University.\u00a0 The Head Coach is expected to serve as the public face of the program, creating and maintaining a positive public image while recruiting and training student-athletes to compete at the highest level possible. This position reports to the Athletics Director. Responsibilities: Develop and implement a comprehensive training program to enhance players' skills, knowledge, and performance in lacrosse. Plan and conduct regular practices, focusing on individual and team development, strategy implementation, and game preparation Provide instruction and guidance to players on proper techniques, rules, and strategies specific to women's lacrosse. Teach and set expectations of appropriate team conduct during competition, travel, practice and any University event, and at any other times when the team is representing the University. Evaluate players' abilities and provide constructive feedback to help them improve their skills and performance. Develop game plans and strategies to maximize the team's chances of success during competitions Ensure compliance with Atlantic East Conference and university policies and procedures. Meet student athlete recruiting goals as established by the Director of Athletics and Recreation Achieve and maintain certification for CPR/AED and First Aid Monitor team fundraising account and ensure accurate coordination and reporting of funds usage and maintenance in accordance with university guidelines Develop and maintain alumni relations for the promotion of the program. Represent the University and its athletics program, with honesty, integrity, and sportsmanship at all times, to various institutional programs and students, parents and families, the general public, alumni and external agencies. Work with various departments and personnel at the university to aid in the development of a positive student-athlete experience. Other duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics and Recreation Immaculata University is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. Requirements: Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's Degree required with high-school or club\u00a0 head coaching experience. Preferred Requirements: College coaching experience a plus. Additional Information: Special Requirements Background check required after a conditional job offer is made. Consideration of the background check will be tailored to the requirements of the job. Application Instructions: Required Documents: Resume Cover Letter Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Immaculata University 1145 KING ROAD IMMACULATA, PA. 19345"}, "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=161063": {"title": "Adjunct - MBA Program", "description": "Immaculata University\nJob Posting: Adjunct  - MBA Program Immaculata University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct  - MBA Program Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct  - MBA Program Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Business Locations: Malvern, PA, PA Posted: Apr 11, 2023 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Contract Position\u00a0ID: 161063 Share About Immaculata University: Immaculata University seeks candidates who are passionate about upholding the value of higher education while fostering institutional excellence. Immaculata University is a comprehensive, co-ed institution of higher learning that has emphasized academic success, student outcomes and faith-based values for more than 100 years. Offering more than 75 in-demand undergraduate, graduate and certificate programs, Immaculata University provides attainable education, personal support and meaningful career pathways to tomorrow's leaders who are focused on intellectual, personal, professional and spiritual growth. Immaculata's expansive suburban campus is located in renowned Chester County, Pennsylvania, 30 miles west of Philadelphia. Job Description: Immaculata University invites applications for adjunct business faculty positions for our new Master's of Business Administration (MBA) program . Candidates interested in developing course material and implementing innovative educational strategies to a diverse student population are encouraged to apply. Courses will be run in an online synchronous format over a 7- week period. Classes to be staffed include: Quantitative Decision Making Financial Analysis for Leaders People and Organizations Emerging Topics in Business Contemporary Marketing Avoiding Organizational Failure Financial Planning The successful candidate will: Create and manage syllabi for courses taught Create lesson plans and execute online synchronous lessons Meet with students during scheduled class meeting times Assess student learning based on quantitative assessment tools Provide students with feedback on assignments in a timely manner Respond to students' questions, and be available to assist students in learning course materials Promote the mission of the business department and Immaculata University Immaculata University is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. Requirements: The ideal candidate will have an earned MBA, teaching experience at the college level, and industry experience in the appropriate field. Preference will be given to candidates with an earned doctorate in a relevant field. Additional Information: Special Requirements Background check required after a conditional job offer is made. Consideration of the background check will be tailored to the requirements of the job. Application Instructions: Required Documents: Resume Cover Letter Copies of transcripts of \u00a0undergraduate and graduate degrees (to be provided upon hire) Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Immaculata University 1145 KING ROAD IMMACULATA, PA. 19345"}, "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=182580": {"title": "Adjunct Clinical Faculty, Division of Nursing", "description": "Immaculata University\nJob Posting: Adjunct Clinical Faculty, Division of Nursing Immaculata University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Clinical Faculty, Division of Nursing Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Clinical Faculty, Division of Nursing Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Nursing - 4 year Locations: Malvern, PA Posted: Oct 29, 2024 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part Time Exempt Ref.\u00a0No.: Job Number 150449 Position\u00a0ID: 182580 Share About Immaculata University: Immaculata University seeks candidates who are passionate about upholding the value of higher education while fostering institutional excellence. Immaculata University is a comprehensive, co-ed institution of higher learning that has emphasized academic success, student outcomes and faith-based values for more than 100 years. Offering more than 75 in-demand undergraduate, graduate and certificate programs, Immaculata University provides attainable education, personal support and meaningful career pathways to tomorrow's leaders who are focused on intellectual, personal, professional and spiritual growth. Immaculata's expansive suburban campus is located in renowned Chester County, Pennsylvania, 30 miles west of Philadelphia. Job Description: Immaculata University invites applications for adjunct clinical faculty positions in the Division of Nursing with our Pre-Licensure BSN and Accelerated BSN Programs. Candidates interested in working with a team to implement innovative educational strategies to a diverse student population are encouraged to apply. Nursing education expertise in all specialties is sought at this time for clinical rotations. Immaculata University is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. Requirements: Current PA Registered Nurse License Master's Degree in Nursing (or in progress) Additional Information: Application review will begin immediately and continue until the positions are filled Multiple adjunct faculty positions available Application Instructions: Required Documents: Cover Letter Current curriculum vitae Three letters of professional references Copies of transcripts of\u00a0undergraduate and graduate degrees (to be provided upon hire) Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Immaculata University 1145 KING ROAD IMMACULATA, PA. 19345"}, "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=179100": {"title": "Adjunct Clinical/Lab Faculty, Division of Nursing", "description": "Immaculata University\nJob Posting: Adjunct Clinical/Lab Faculty, Division of Nursing Immaculata University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Clinical/Lab Faculty, Division of Nursing Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Clinical/Lab Faculty, Division of Nursing Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Nursing - 4 year Locations: Malvern, PA Posted: Jul 24, 2024 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part Time Exempt Ref.\u00a0No.: Job Number 150449 Position\u00a0ID: 179100 Share About Immaculata University: Immaculata University seeks candidates who are passionate about upholding the value of higher education while fostering institutional excellence. Immaculata University is a comprehensive, co-ed institution of higher learning that has emphasized academic success, student outcomes and faith-based values for more than 100 years. Offering more than 75 in-demand undergraduate, graduate and certificate programs, Immaculata University provides attainable education, personal support and meaningful career pathways to tomorrow's leaders who are focused on intellectual, personal, professional and spiritual growth. Immaculata's expansive suburban campus is located in renowned Chester County, Pennsylvania, 30 miles west of Philadelphia. Job Description: Immaculata University invites applications for adjunct clinical faculty positions in the Division of Nursing with our Pre-Licensure BSN and Accelerated BSN Programs. Candidates interested in working with a team to implement innovative educational strategies to a diverse student population are encouraged to apply. Nursing education expertise in all specialties is sought at this time for clinical rotations and lab instruction. Immaculata University is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. Requirements: Current PA Registered Nurse License Master's Degree in Nursing (or in progress) Additional Information: Application review will begin immediately and continue until the positions are filled Multiple adjunct faculty positions available Application Instructions: Required Documents: Cover Letter Current curriculum vitae Three letters of professional references Copies of transcripts of\u00a0undergraduate and graduate degrees (to be provided upon hire) Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Immaculata University 1145 KING ROAD IMMACULATA, PA. 19345"}, "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=202668": {"title": "Adjunct English Composition Instructor", "description": "Im