l Psychology. Multicultural and diversity awareness and scholarly commitment in this area is highly preferred. Immaculata University's Psy.D. Program is committed to hiring individuals from diverse backgrounds and creating an inclusive environment. Responsibilities: Working with doctoral students to include teaching, advisement, and supervising dissertations Other departmental responsibilities as assigned Immaculata University is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. Requirements: Minimum Requirements: Doctorate in clinical psychology and licensed as a psychologist in Pennsylvania Preferred Requirements: Teaching experience is preferred. Additional Information: Special Requirements Background check required after a conditional job offer is made. Consideration of the background check will be tailored to the requirements of the job. Application Instructions: Required Documents: Resume Cover Letter Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Immaculata University 1145 KING ROAD IMMACULATA, PA. 19345"}, "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204845": {"title": "Diagnostic Medical Sonography Program Director/Associate Faculty, Full-time", "description": "Immaculata University\nJob Posting: Diagnostic Medical Sonography Program Director/Associate Faculty, Full-time Immaculata University \n\tJob Posting: Diagnostic Medical Sonography Program Director/Associate Faculty, Full-time Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Diagnostic Medical Sonography Program Director/Associate Faculty, Full-time Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Dept of Health Science and Services Locations: Malvern, PA Posted: Sep 15, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full Time Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 204845 Share About Immaculata University: Immaculata University seeks candidates who are passionate about upholding the value of higher education while fostering institutional excellence. Immaculata University is a comprehensive, co-ed institution of higher learning that has emphasized academic success, student outcomes and faith-based values for more than 100 years. Offering more than 75 in-demand undergraduate, graduate and certificate programs, Immaculata University provides attainable education, personal support and meaningful career pathways to tomorrow's leaders who are focused on intellectual, personal, professional and spiritual growth. Immaculata's expansive suburban campus is located in renowned Chester County, Pennsylvania, 30 miles west of Philadelphia. Why Immaculata University is the Perfect Workplace for you: Collegial Atmosphere, caring leadership, work/life balance. Mission-driven values supported by five core values: faith, community, knowledge, virtue and service. Generous paid time off benefits. Tuition Assistance: You, your spouse, and your eligible dependent children can receive tuition assistance at IU.\u00a0 Your dependent children are also eligible for tuition assistance at other institutions via the Tuition Exchange program. Health. Life, and Disability Insurance: Prescription, Dental, Vision, and Life Insurance; Disability benefits, Flexible Spending Account and Health Savings Account. Retirement Plan: Generous retirement plan to help you save for your future. Job Description: Immaculata University invites applications for a full-time Associate Faculty position with the responsibilities as the Program Director for the Diagnostic Medical Sonography program within the Department of Health, Nutrition, and Exercise Sciences (HNES). The Program Director position is responsible for managing and supervising all operations related to Diagnostic Medical Sonography (DMS). This role includes oversight of program accreditation, faculty development, curriculum design, and student success while ensuring compliance with regulatory and accreditation standards. The target start date is January 2027. Responsibilities: Oversee the structure and daily operations of the program, including organization, administration, periodic review, evaluation, ongoing development, and overall effectiveness of the program curricula Ensure the quality and effectiveness of all clinical affiliates and clinical education centers are maintained Ensure educational responsibilities are not compromised by non-educational functions Promote and ensure valid evaluations of students by clinical instructors, department managers, staff sonographers, and peers Collect and analyze student data to monitor retention rates, credential pass rates, and feedback from employer and student surveys Ensure the program meets the accreditation standards set by CAAHEP and remains viable and compliant Develop and implement program-specific policies that align with accreditation requirements Develop and manage the annual programmatic budget with input from faculty and provide documentation for approved expenditures Recruit, screen, and facilitate the employment of qualified adjunct and full-time faculty in coordination with the Chair of HNES Assist in student recruitment, advisement, and registration Prepare syllabi annually, and coordinate syllabi and course content to meet program goals Collaborate with the Chair of HNES to determine effective courses schedules and the appropriate faculty for course assignments Manage labs and facilities to meet students' learning need Promote the DMS program through participation in university open houses, community events, outreach activities, and public relations efforts Serve as a liaison between the university and clinical agencies, fostering effective communication and collaboration with the Clinical Coordinator Collaborate with the Clinical Coordinator to oversee clinical education, including securing and maintaining clinical sites, developing schedules, and ensuring appropriate supervision and competency evaluation for students Maintain accurate student clinical records in collaboration with the Clinical Coordinator, including calculating and reporting quarterly grades Ensure all program documentation (brochures, website, catalog, and handbook) is accurate and up to date Coordinate advisory committee membership, meetings and minutes. Maintain knowledge of current industry practices and integrate updated methods into the curriculum Participate in university committees, and Department of Health, Nutrition, and Exercise Sciences and campus events to support institutional goals and community engagement Perform additional duties as assigned by the departmental chair and dean Immaculata University is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. Requirements: Minimum Requirements: Baccalaureate degree Registered Diagnostic Medical Sonographer with Abdomen (AB) specialty and Obstetrics and Gynecology (OB/GYN) specialty as administered by American Registry for Diagnostic Medical Sonography (ARDMS) Appropriate credential(s) specific to one or more of the concentrations(s) offered Documented experience in supervision, instruction, evaluation, student guidance, and educational theories and techniques; Minimum of three years of clinical experience as a registered sonographer in the professional sonography field. Preferred Requirements: Master's degree Sonography curriculum development, implementation, revision, and program assessment Accreditation standards and guidelines for sonography programs Registered in Vascular and Echocardiology specialties (RDCS/RCS or RVS/RVT). Additional Information: Special Requirements Background check required after a conditional job offer is made. Consideration of the background check will be tailored to the requirements of the job. Application Instructions: Required Documents: Resume Cover Letter Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Immaculata University 1145 KING ROAD IMMACULATA, PA. 19345"}, "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=202909": {"title": "Full-time, Tenure Track Faculty - Division of Nursing", "description": "Immaculata University\nJob Posting: Full-time, Tenure Track Faculty - Division of Nursing Immaculata University \n\tJob Posting: Full-time, Tenure Track Faculty - Division of Nursing Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Full-time, Tenure Track Faculty - Division of Nursing Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Nursing - 4 year Locations: Malvern, PA Posted: Jul 22, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full Time Exempt Ref.\u00a0No.: Job ID: 200336/Reg#: 346825 Position\u00a0ID: 202909 Share About Immaculata University: Immaculata University seeks candidates who are passionate about upholding the value of higher education while fostering institutional excellence. Immaculata University is a comprehensive, co-ed institution of higher learning that has emphasized academic success, student outcomes and faith-based values for more than 100 years. Offering more than 75 in-demand undergraduate, graduate and certificate programs, Immaculata University provides attainable education, personal support and meaningful career pathways to tomorrow's leaders who are focused on intellectual, personal, professional and spiritual growth. Immaculata's expansive suburban campus is located in renowned Chester County, Pennsylvania, 30 miles west of Philadelphia. Why Immaculata University is the Perfect Workplace for you: Collegial Atmosphere, caring leadership, work/life balance. Mission-driven values supported by five core values: faith, community, knowledge, virtue and service. Tuition Assistance: You, your spouse, and your eligible dependent children can receive tuition assistance at IU.\u00a0 Your dependent children are also eligible for tuition assistance at other institutions via the Tuition Exchange program. Health. Life, and Disability Insurance: Prescription, Dental, Vision, and Life Insurance; Disability benefits, Flexible Spending Account and Health Savings Account. Retirement Plan: Generous retirement plan to help you save for your future. Job Description: Summary: Immaculata University invites applications for full-time tenure track positions in the Division of Nursing with a pre-licensure BSN, RN to BSN and MSN programs. MSN and earned doctorate in nursing or related field required with teaching experience in undergraduate program highly desirable. Candidates, interested in working with a team to implement innovative educational strategies to a diverse student population, are encouraged to apply. Nursing education expertise particularly in the areas of Psychiatric Mental Health, Pediatrics/Obstetrics, Pharmacology, and Pathophysiology is sought. Responsibilities include didactic and clinical teaching, student advisement, curriculum development, support of the university's mission and vision, scholarship and service through participation in division, university and professional activities. The anticipated start for this role is January 2027. Responsibilities: Develop and deliver undergraduate and/or graduate nursing courses, ensuring that content is current and aligns with accreditation standards. Design and implement assessments to evaluate student learning outcomes effectively. Participate in the ongoing implementation, evaluation, and enhancement of the undergraduate nursing program to reflect CCNE, AACN, and SBON standards, current evidence and best practices. Teach across the nursing programs as assigned by the Division of Nursing Chair. Provide academic advising to nursing students and mentor them in their professional development. Participate in university committees, and Division of Nursing and campus events to support institutional goals and community engagement. Perform additional duties as assigned by the Division Chair and Dean. Immaculata University is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. Requirements: Minimum Requirements: Doctoral degree in Nursing or Master of Science in Nursing with a doctoral degree in a related field* An unencumbered registered nurse license in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) is required Preferred Requirements: Experience with teaching didactic, clinical, and lab courses. Experience with nursing labs and/or simulation labs is preferred. *A candidate with an MSN will qualify for the rank of instructor. A candidate with an MSN and a doctorate will qualify for the rank of assistant professor Additional Information: Special Requirements Background check required after a conditional job offer is made. Consideration of the background check will be tailored to the requirements of the job. Application Instructions: Required Documents: Resume Cover Letter Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Immaculata University 1145 KING ROAD IMMACULATA, PA. 19345"}, "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204404": {"title": "Maintenance Tech III - Plumber", "description": "Immaculata University\nJob Posting: Maintenance Tech III - Plumber Immaculata University \n\tJob Posting: Maintenance Tech III - Plumber Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Maintenance Tech III - Plumber Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Facilities Locations: Malvern, PA Posted: Sep 2, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full Time Non Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 204404 Share About Immaculata University: Immaculata University seeks candidates who are passionate about upholding the value of higher education while fostering institutional excellence. Immaculata University is a comprehensive, co-ed institution of higher learning that has emphasized academic success, student outcomes and faith-based values for more than 100 years. Offering more than 75 in-demand undergraduate, graduate and certificate programs, Immaculata University provides attainable education, personal support and meaningful career pathways to tomorrow's leaders who are focused on intellectual, personal, professional and spiritual growth. Immaculata's expansive suburban campus is located in renowned Chester County, Pennsylvania, 30 miles west of Philadelphia. Why Immaculata University is the Perfect Workplace for you: Collegial Atmosphere, caring leadership, work/life balance. Mission-driven values supported by five core values: faith, community, knowledge, virtue and service. Generous paid time off benefits. Tuition Assistance: You, your spouse, and your eligible dependent children can receive tuition assistance at IU.\u00a0 Your dependent children are also eligible for tuition assistance at other institutions via the Tuition Exchange program. Health. Life, and Disability Insurance: Prescription, Dental, Vision, and Life Insurance; Disability benefits, Flexible Spending Account and Health Savings Account. Retirement Plan: Generous retirement plan to help you save for your future. Job Description: The Maintenance Technician III ? Plumber is responsible for the installation, maintenance, repair, and inspection of plumbing systems and related equipment throughout the university campus. This position ensures that all plumbing infrastructure operates safely, efficiently, and in compliance with applicable codes and regulations. The successful candidate will support the university's mission by providing exceptional service to students, faculty, staff, and guests. Responsibilities: Install, maintain, troubleshoot, and repair commercial and residential plumbing systems. Repair and replace water lines, drain lines, valves, fixtures, pumps, water heaters, and related plumbing equipment. Diagnose plumbing issues and determine appropriate corrective actions. Perform preventative maintenance on plumbing systems and equipment. Respond to emergency plumbing calls, including water leaks, clogged drains, and system failures. Inspect plumbing systems for compliance with local, state, and federal regulations. Maintain accurate records of work performed, materials used, and preventative maintenance activities. Assist with campus renovation and construction projects as assigned. Coordinate with contractors and vendors when necessary. Support other maintenance trades during peak workloads or emergency situations. Maintain a safe work environment and follow all university safety policies and procedures. Participate in on-call rotation and after-hours emergency response as required. Immaculata University is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. Requirements: Minimum Requirements: High school diploma or equivalent. Journeyman Plumber license preferred or equivalent documented experience. Minimum of five (5) years of commercial plumbing experience. Working knowledge of plumbing codes, regulations, and industry standards. Ability to read blueprints, schematics, and technical drawings. Valid driver's license with an acceptable driving record. Ability to operate tools, equipment, and vehicles required for the position. Strong troubleshooting and problem-solving skills. Ability to prioritize multiple tasks and respond effectively to emergencies. Excellent communication and customer service skills. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Knowledge of occupational safety practices and procedures Preferred Requirements: Experience working in educational, healthcare, or institutional facilities. Backflow certification is a plus. Experience with steam systems, boilers, and hydronic systems. Experience with computerized maintenance management systems (CMMS). Physical Requirements: Ability to lift and carry up to 75 pounds. Ability to climb ladders, work in confined spaces, and perform duties at various heights. Ability to frequently stand, walk, bend, kneel, crawl, and work outdoors in varying weather conditions. Ability to respond to emergency situations during evenings, weekends, and holidays when required. Additional Information: Special Requirements Background check required after a conditional job offer is made. Consideration of the background check will be tailored to the requirements of the job. Application Instructions: Required Documents: Resume Cover Letter Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Immaculata University 1145 KING ROAD IMMACULATA, PA. 19345"}, "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=201379": {"title": "Maintenance Tech III / HVAC", "description": "Immaculata University\nJob Posting: Maintenance Tech III / HVAC Immaculata University \n\tJob Posting: Maintenance Tech III / HVAC Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Maintenance Tech III / HVAC Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Facilities Locations: Malvern, PA Posted: Jun 10, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full Time Non Exempt Ref.\u00a0No.: Orig Req 344145/ Job ID: 197929 Position\u00a0ID: 201379 Share About Immaculata University: Immaculata University seeks candidates who are passionate about upholding the value of higher education while fostering institutional excellence. Immaculata University is a comprehensive, co-ed institution of higher learning that has emphasized academic success, student outcomes and faith-based values for more than 100 years. Offering more than 75 in-demand undergraduate, graduate and certificate programs, Immaculata University provides attainable education, personal support and meaningful career pathways to tomorrow's leaders who are focused on intellectual, personal, professional and spiritual growth. Immaculata's expansive suburban campus is located in renowned Chester County, Pennsylvania, 30 miles west of Philadelphia. Why Immaculata University is the Perfect Workplace for you: Collegial Atmosphere, caring leadership, work/life balance. Mission-driven values supported by five core values: faith, community, knowledge, virtue and service. Generous paid time off benefits. Tuition Assistance: You, your spouse, and your eligible dependent children can receive tuition assistance at IU.\u00a0 Your dependent children are also eligible for tuition assistance at other institutions via the Tuition Exchange program. Health. Life, and Disability Insurance: Prescription, Dental, Vision, and Life Insurance; Disability benefits, Flexible Spending Account and Health Savings Account. Retirement Plan: Generous retirement plan to help you save for your future. Job Description: This position will perform tasks related to maintaining and improving the facility mechanical systems. To provide a safe, functional, and attractive environment for the campus' students, faculty, staff, administrators, and visitors. Responsibilities: Maintain, install, troubleshoot and repair the campus HVAC equipment. Equipment includes but not limited to boilers (steam and hot water),Chillers, cooling towers, air handling units, VAV devices, pumps, hot water\u00a0 heaters, air compressors, motor centers, electrical panels, transformers, automatic doors,\u00a0 electrical actuators, vacuum pumps, fans, dehumidifiers/humidifiers, refrigeration equipment,\u00a0 air conditioners, \u00a0kitchen equipment, lighting, generators, fire alarms, and water coolers. Will perform HVAC work and troubleshooting. Provide on-call and after hours coverage. Assist the mechanical and general maintenance men. Assist the Facilities Department in the removal of snow on campus. Operate light or medium weight trucks and equipment to include tractors and snow removal equipment. Work as directed by the Facility Management. Remain up-to-date and informed as to current practices of job related functions. Work with other people that may be contacted in an agreeable manner. Cooperate with other people within the department and other department personnel in completing assigned tasks. Display the necessary initiative and dependability to work alone or in groups. Perform all duties in a safe and professional manner and in accordance with department policies and procedures. Complete daily work orders and PM's. Turn in completed paperwork at the end of each shift worked. Ensure pool, boiler, chiller, waste water treatment plant, mechanical, and water inspections and maintenance are completed and logged daily. Ensure service slips, packing slips, and completed paperwork back to the Facilities office daily. Ensure that all work is being conducted in a safe and ethical manner. Complete daily safety inspections. Responsible for working in compliance with all OSHA, EPA, and other local, state, and federal government laws and regulations. Perform any additional duties to support Immaculata University as deemed necessary. Ability to work nights, weekends, and holidays as needed. Immaculata University is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. Requirements: Minimum Requirements: Formal HVAC vocational, technical or apprenticeship training or five years of HVAC experience. Able to read and comprehend blueprints. Must have basic computer knowledge to include Microsoft Outlook, Word, and Excel. Good health with adequate strength and endurance to perform the work described in various types of weather. Deal with employees, management, and clients guests and employees with tact and courtesy. Possess a valid driver's license. Subject to MVR check. Ability to follow oral and written instructions. Ability to maintain effective relations with supervisor and fellow employees. Ability to follow and apply safety rules and regulations for job assignments and equipment used. Ability to lift and carry items weighing 50 pounds. Ability to use tools and equipment as required. Eighteen (18) years of age or older. Willing to be trained as required. Additional Information: Special Requirements Background check required after a conditional job offer is made. Consideration of the background check will be tailored to the requirements of the job. Application Instructions: Required Documents: Resume Cover Letter Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Immaculata University 1145 KING ROAD IMMACULATA, PA. 19345"}, "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=202667": {"title": "Nursing Clinical Coordinator - Division of Nursing", "description": "Immaculata University\nJob Posting: Nursing Clinical Coordinator - Division of Nursing Immaculata University \n\tJob Posting: Nursing Clinical Coordinator - Division of Nursing Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Nursing Clinical Coordinator - Division of Nursing Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Nursing - 4 year Locations: Malvern, PA Posted: Jul 15, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full Time Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 202667 Share About Immaculata University: Immaculata University seeks candidates who are passionate about upholding the value of higher education while fostering institutional excellence. Immaculata University is a comprehensive, co-ed institution of higher learning that has emphasized academic success, student outcomes and faith-based values for more than 100 years. Offering more than 75 in-demand undergraduate, graduate and certificate programs, Immaculata University provides attainable education, personal support and meaningful career pathways to tomorrow's leaders who are focused on intellectual, personal, professional and spiritual growth. Immaculata's expansive suburban campus is located in renowned Chester County, Pennsylvania, 30 miles west of Philadelphia. Why Immaculata University is the Perfect Workplace for you: Collegial Atmosphere, caring leadership, work/life balance. Mission-driven values supported by five core values: faith, community, knowledge, virtue and service. Generous paid time off benefits. Tuition Assistance: You, your spouse, and your eligible dependent children can receive tuition assistance at IU.\u00a0 Your dependent children are also eligible for tuition assistance at other institutions via the Tuition Exchange program. Health. Life, and Disability Insurance: Prescription, Dental, Vision, and Life Insurance; Disability benefits, Flexible Spending Account and Health Savings Account. Retirement Plan: Generous retirement plan to help you save for your future. Job Description: Immaculata University invites applications for a full-time Nursing Clinical Coordinator. This role is responsible for the comprehensive coordination, organization, and oversight of undergraduate nursing student clinical and lab rotations and the procurement of necessary instructional faculty. The Coordinator serves as a vital liaison among the nursing program, healthcare partners, and regulatory bodies to ensure all clinical learning environments and faculty staffing meet program outcomes and Pennsylvania Board of Nursing (PA BON) requirements. The Clinical Coordinator collaborates with program leadership and clinical partners to facilitate student placements, maintain clinical affiliation requirements, and support the effective delivery of clinical education experiences. Responsibilities: Coordinate undergraduate nursing student clinical and lab placements across affiliated healthcare agencies and clinical practice settings. Maintain clinical rotation schedules, placement records, and student assignment information. Collaborate with healthcare agencies to secure and confirm clinical placements that align with course and program objectives. Coordinate onboarding requirements for clinical placements including orientation schedules, agency-specific requirements, and access procedures. Assist in balancing student placements to ensure appropriate clinical capacity and learning opportunities. Serve as a primary contact between the nursing program and affiliated clinical agencies. Maintain positive working relationships with clinical partners, nurse managers, educators, and preceptors. Communicate program expectations, schedules, and placement needs to clinical agencies in a timely manner. Participate in meetings with healthcare partners regarding clinical education operations and partnership development. Assist with maintaining and monitoring clinical affiliation agreements, as directed. Collaborate with course faculty and program leadership regarding clinical scheduling, placement needs, and site-specific requirements. Assist students with clinical onboarding processes and provide guidance related to clinical placement expectations. Communicate clinical schedules, assignments, and updates to students and faculty. Address and escalate clinical placement concerns or scheduling conflicts, as appropriate. Support orientation activities for students entering clinical settings. Verify with the compliance coordinator that students assigned to clinical rotations meet institutional, agency, and PA Board of Nursing clinical compliance requirements prior to placement. Maintain accurate records related to clinical placements, agency requirements, and student assignments. Assist with preparation of reports and documentation for accreditation reviews, audits, and program evaluation activities. Ensure adherence to policies and standards established by clinical agencies, regulatory bodies, and accrediting organizations Assist with evaluating clinical site utilization and identifying opportunities for expanded partnerships. Support continuous improvement initiatives related to clinical education operations and processes. Perform additional duties related to clinical education coordination as assigned. Provides clinical site educators and students with materials, including division of nursing policies, information or clinical site orientation, address, contact person, phone numbers, and parking information Responsible for onboarding procedure for newly hired adjunct faculty Communicates with business office concerning certificates of insurance and affiliation agreements. Participate in Division of Nursing and campus events to support institutional goals and community engagement. Collaborate with the Division of Nursing (DON) Chair and the Assistant Director of Lab/Clinical to conduct regular site visits to evaluate the quality of clinical environments. Perform additional duties as assigned by the Division Chair and Dean. Immaculata University is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. Requirements: Minimum Requirements: Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) required. Current unencumbered Registered Nurse (RN) license in Commonwealth of Pennsylvania Minimum of 2 years of clinical nursing experience. Strong organizational and communication skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite and database or scheduling systems. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, students, and healthcare partners. Preferred Requirements: MSN in Nursing preferred, or willingness to obtain. Experience in nursing education, clinical instruction, or student placement coordination. Knowledge of undergraduate nursing clinical education requirements and accreditation standards. Experience working with healthcare systems and clinical affiliation processes. Familiarity with clinical scheduling or placement software systems. Additional Information: Special Requirements Background check required after a conditional job offer is made. Consideration of the background check will be tailored to the requirements of the job. Application Instructions: Required Documents: Resume Cover Letter Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Immaculata University 1145 KING ROAD IMMACULATA, PA. 19345"}, "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204429": {"title": "Part-Time Assistant Coach - Softball", "description": "Immaculata University\nJob Posting: Part-Time Assistant Coach - Softball Immaculata University \n\tJob Posting: Part-Time Assistant Coach - Softball Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Part-Time Assistant Coach - Softball Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Athletics Locations: Malvern, PA Posted: Sep 3, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Contract Position\u00a0ID: 204429 Share About Immaculata University: Immaculata University seeks candidates who are passionate about upholding the value of higher education while fostering institutional excellence. Immaculata University is a comprehensive, co-ed institution of higher learning that has emphasized academic success, student outcomes and faith-based values for more than 100 years. Offering more than 75 in-demand undergraduate, graduate and certificate programs, Immaculata University provides attainable education, personal support and meaningful career pathways to tomorrow's leaders who are focused on intellectual, personal, professional and spiritual growth. Immaculata's expansive suburban campus is located in renowned Chester County, Pennsylvania, 30 miles west of Philadelphia. Why Immaculata University is the Perfect Workplace for you: Collegial Atmosphere, caring leadership, work/life balance. Mission-driven values supported by five core values: faith, community, knowledge, virtue and service. Job Description: The Part-Time Assistant Softball Coach will assist the Head Coach with practices, games, player development, recruiting, and overall team operations. The ideal candidate will have strong softball knowledge, communication skills, and a commitment to developing college student-athletes. Responsibilities: Assist with planning and conducting team practices and workouts. Provide instruction and development in softball fundamentals and position-specific skills. Assist with game preparation, in-game coaching, scouting, and team strategy. Support recruiting efforts, camps, clinics, and team events as needed. Help maintain a positive, competitive, and professional team environment. Availability & Travel: Must be available to participate in most team practices throughout the season. Must have flexibility for games, tournaments, evenings, and weekends as needed. Required availability for the team Immaculata University is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. Requirements: Minimum Requirements: Previous softball playing or coaching experience required. Strong knowledge of softball fundamentals and strategy. Ability to work effectively with college-aged student-athletes. Strong communication, organizational, and teamwork skills. Preferred Requirements: Collegiate softball coaching or playing experience preferred. Additional Information: Special Requirements Background check required after a conditional job offer is made. Consideration of the background check will be tailored to the requirements of the job. Application Instructions: Required Documents: Resume Cover Letter Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Immaculata University 1145 KING ROAD IMMACULATA, PA. 19345"}, "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205563": {"title": "Security officer (FT)", "description": "Immaculata University\nJob Posting: Security officer (FT) Immaculata University \n\tJob Posting: Security officer (FT) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Security officer (FT) Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Security Locations: Malvern, PA Posted: Oct 6, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full Time Non Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 205563 Share About Immaculata University: Immaculata University seeks candidates who are passionate about upholding the value of higher education while fostering institutional excellence. Immaculata University is a comprehensive, co-ed institution of higher learning that has emphasized academic success, student outcomes and faith-based values for more than 100 years. Offering more than 75 in-demand undergraduate, graduate and certificate programs, Immaculata University provides attainable education, personal support and meaningful career pathways to tomorrow's leaders who are focused on intellectual, personal, professional and spiritual growth. Immaculata's expansive suburban campus is located in renowned Chester County, Pennsylvania, 30 miles west of Philadelphia. Why Immaculata University is the Perfect Workplace for you: Collegial Atmosphere, caring leadership, work/life balance. Mission-driven values supported by five core values: faith, community, knowledge, virtue and service. Generous paid time off benefits. Tuition Assistance: You, your spouse, and your eligible dependent children can receive tuition assistance at IU.\u00a0 Your dependent children are also eligible for tuition assistance at other institutions via the Tuition Exchange program. Health. Life, and Disability Insurance: Prescription, Dental, Vision, and Life Insurance; Disability benefits, Flexible Spending Account and Health Savings Account. Retirement Plan: Generous retirement plan to help you save for your future. Job Description: Provide preventative and investigative security services for students, staff, and visitors of the University.\u00a0 Maintain safety and security of the University community. This position reports to the Director of Safety and Protection. Responsibilities: Maintain Security and Safety Enforce criminal and parking laws and administrative regulations Demonstrate analytical skills in applying law and regulations Knowledge of criminal and traffic laws and administration regulations Internal/external, walking and driving patrols of campus and facilities Escort students, faculty, and staff as required Lock and secure buildings Prepare written incident reports and maintain activity logs Demonstrate timeliness and thoroughness in completing rounds Provide Emergency Services as Required Crisis intervention Demonstrates knowledge and training in emergency situations Provides First Aid assistance as needed Customer Service: Provide information/direction to students, faculty, staff and visitors Demonstrate good judgment in applying law and policy regulations Demonstrate cooperation / teamwork in carrying out assignments Immaculata University is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. Requirements: Minimum Requirements: Excellent report writing skills Strong interpersonal and communication skills Good judgment\u00a0skills and ability to remain calm in situations / crisis Computer skills including ability to use email, Microsoft software (including Outlook, Word, Teams, etc.) Ability to sit, stand and walk for extended time periods Able to lift and carry up to 50 pounds Ability to work in both indoor and outdoor environments in a variety of weather conditions and temperatures CPR and First Aid training helpful Possess a valid driver's license. Subject to MVR check. High school diploma or equivalent Preferred Requirements: Prior Security experience working in a Higher Education setting. Additional Information: Special Requirements: Background check required after a conditional job offer is made. Consideration of the background check will be tailored to the requirements of the job. Application Instructions: Required Documents: Resume Cover Letter Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Immaculata University 1145 KING ROAD IMMACULATA, PA. 19345"}, "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203030": {"title": "Volunteer Assistant Coach Men's Lacrosse", "description": "Immaculata University\nJob Posting: Volunteer Assistant Coach Men's Lacrosse Immaculata University \n\tJob Posting: Volunteer Assistant Coach Men's Lacrosse Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Volunteer Assistant Coach Men's Lacrosse Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Athletics Locations: Malvern, PA Posted: Jul 27, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Contract Position\u00a0ID: 203030 Share About Immaculata University: Immaculata University seeks candidates who are passionate about upholding the value of higher education while fostering institutional excellence. Immaculata University is a comprehensive, co-ed institution of higher learning that has emphasized academic success, student outcomes and faith-based values for more than 100 years. Offering more than 75 in-demand undergraduate, graduate and certificate programs, Immaculata University provides attainable education, personal support and meaningful career pathways to tomorrow's leaders who are focused on intellectual, personal, professional and spiritual growth. Immaculata's expansive suburban campus is located in renowned Chester County, Pennsylvania, 30 miles west of Philadelphia. Why Immaculata University is the Perfect Workplace for you: Collegial Atmosphere, caring leadership, work/life balance. Mission-driven values supported by five core values: faith, community, knowledge, virtue and service. Job Description: The Volunteer Assistant Men's Lacrosse Coach assists the Head Coach in all aspects of operating a NCAA Division III men's lacrosse program. This position supports the development of student-athletes academically, athletically, and personally while promoting the mission and values of the institution. This is an unpaid volunteer position that provides valuable collegiate coaching experience. Responsibilities: Assist with planning and conducting daily practices and training sessions. Provide position-specific instruction and skill development. Support game-day preparation, including scouting, film analysis, and opponent breakdown. Assist with practice planning, equipment setup, and field preparation. Travel with the team to away contests as assigned. Help identify and evaluate prospective student-athletes in accordance with NCAA Division III and institutional recruiting guidelines. Build positive relationships with current student-athletes and foster a culture of accountability, sportsmanship, and teamwork. Assist with video editing, statistical analysis, and recruiting databases. Support program operations, including camps, clinics, fundraising initiatives, and community engagement activities. Perform additional duties as assigned by the Head Coach. The Volunteer Assistant Coach is expected to understand and comply with all NCAA Division III, conference, and institutional rules and regulations and to uphold the highest standards of integrity and sportsmanship. Immaculata University is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. Requirements: Minimum Requirements: Strong knowledge of lacrosse fundamentals, strategy, and NCAA Division III rules. Excellent communication, organizational, and leadership skills. Ability to work evenings, weekends, holidays, and travel as required during the competitive season. Commitment to fostering an inclusive and positive student-athlete experience. Preferred Requirements: Collegiate playing or coaching experience in men's lacrosse preferred. Additional Information: Special Requirements Background check required after a conditional job offer is made. Consideration of the background check will be tailored to the requirements of the job. Application Instructions: Required Documents: Resume Cover Letter Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Immaculata University 1145 KING ROAD IMMACULATA, PA. 19345"}}, "rows": {"https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204689": {"school_id": 1164, "posting_url": "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204689", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Director of Residence Life", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Residence Life", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204115": {"school_id": 1164, "posting_url": "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204115", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant to the Director of Clinical Training", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Clinical Training", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205901": {"school_id": 1164, "posting_url": "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205901", "job_title_in_post": "Network Administrator", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204724": {"school_id": 1164, "posting_url": "https://immaculata.int